1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:03,086
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:14,848
<i>-There's a spy in Diego's camp?</i>
<i>-We're a political family.</i>

3
00:00:14,931 --> 00:00:18,143
<i>We have been doing this for many years.</i>

4
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:21,771
<i>It doesn't matter who's up against the</i>
<i>Ardientes because we're gonna win.</i>

5
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,398
[Senator Magno] <i>I would love</i>
<i>to get to know</i>

6
00:00:23,481 --> 00:00:24,357
<i>your other son better.</i>

7
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:26,943
<i>Well excuse me, Senator,</i>
<i>but he's not my son,</i>

8
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:30,530
<i>and I cannot believe that you're</i>
<i>even considering that bastard.</i>

9
00:00:30,613 --> 00:00:34,868
<i>I'm giving you until tonight</i>
<i>to finish your job.</i>

10
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:37,328
<i>Or else, do you see that toilet?</i>

11
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:42,208
<i>That's the last thing you'll see before</i>
<i>you die, you piece of shit!</i>

12
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:43,209
<i>Miss Ivy.</i>

13
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:46,212
<i>Where can I find Jaguar?</i>

14
00:00:46,296 --> 00:00:48,173
<i>At the old hideout in the town of Gulod.</i>

15
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:49,799
[gunshot]

16
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:51,342
[Julio] <i>I'm here! Face me.</i>

17
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:53,720
[gunfire]

18
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:56,431
[Rufo] <i>My boss promised</i>
<i>to send us more men.</i>

19
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:59,517
<i>People who can help us gain</i>
<i>more money and power.</i>

20
00:00:59,601 --> 00:01:01,978
<i>-I need to meet him.</i>
<i>-In due time.</i>

21
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:04,189
[Camia] <i>Lily, Senator Magno chose Diego!</i>

22
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:05,690
[Ivy] <i>That's great news!</i>

23
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:10,320
[Camia] <i>Thanks for helping out</i>
<i>with Diego's campaign.</i>

24
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:12,072
[Ivy] <i>Where is he? Let me talk to him.</i>

25
00:01:12,155 --> 00:01:13,615
[Camia] <i>He's not around…</i>

26
00:01:13,698 --> 00:01:14,991
[Emilia] <i>Do you have an update on Camia?</i>

27
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:19,454
[Ivy] <i>Just now, someone called Emilia</i>
<i>while we were on the phone.</i>

28
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:21,664
<i>They planted a spy in your camp.</i>

29
00:01:21,748 --> 00:01:24,459
[Nimfa] <i>Camia does have a backer.</i>
<i>It's not Ivy Aguas.</i>

30
00:01:24,542 --> 00:01:27,670
<i>It's Camia's daughter, Lily Cruz!</i>

31
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:31,382
<i>You heard me! Lily Cruz is alive!</i>

32
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:34,010
[Emilia] <i>Lily Cruz is dead! She's dead!</i>

33
00:01:34,093 --> 00:01:36,387
[Camia] <i>Emilia planted a spy in our camp.</i>

34
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:38,139
<i>And there's only one person I suspect.</i>

35
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:39,057
[Diego] <i>Is it Nimfa?</i>

36
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:40,683
[Camia] <i>Diego, we need to investigate her.</i>

37
00:01:40,767 --> 00:01:44,354
[Emilia] <i>I'll find Lily Cruz</i>
<i>no matter where she's hiding.</i>

38
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:53,404
[Nimfa] Here you go. You get extra pieces

39
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:56,407
as a sign of my gratitude
for defending me earlier.

40
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:59,077
Nimfa, I just noticed something.

41
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:02,080
It's like Miss Camia
doesn't like you that much.

42
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:07,836
I don't get it either.
It makes me feel sad.

43
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:13,216
Because no matter
how nice you are to a person,

44
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:17,303
when they have a bad impression of you,
there's nothing you can do.

45
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:21,683
Well, maybe Miss Camia is just being wary.

46
00:02:21,766 --> 00:02:25,770
Actually, all of us who support
Diego are like that too.

47
00:02:26,271 --> 00:02:27,063
Who knows?

48
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:31,568
Someone from the opposing party
might be spying on us.

49
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:35,071
We can't help but be really cautious.
But you know what?

50
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:38,741
Don't worry about that.
Let's just chill for now.

51
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:43,288
-Chill?
-Mm-hm. Chill.

52
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:47,000
Because it looks like
this will take a while.

53
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:49,919
Wait, let me order more. Miss?

54
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:52,088
Three more bottles of beer, please.

55
00:02:52,171 --> 00:02:53,840
Give them all to this woman.

56
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:56,009
[chuckles]

57
00:02:56,092 --> 00:02:57,886
-Let's just have a toast!
-All right.

58
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:02,807
[Ivy] Yes, I want to know
everything about Lily Cruz.

59
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:07,896
I want info immediately.
Do you understand? Thank you.

60
00:03:09,981 --> 00:03:12,400
Are you sure you want
to help Mom with this?

61
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:14,861
Of course, Arnaldo.

62
00:03:15,778 --> 00:03:18,656
I need to help my future mother-in-law.

63
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:21,784
You know what, hon?

64
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:25,747
To be honest, I think Lily Cruz is dead.

65
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,790
Because if she were alive…

66
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:33,171
why would she let her mother
expose herself, right?

67
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:40,261
Well, anyway… Hon, I just want to ask you.

68
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:46,643
Do you think Emilia really
trusts her spy on Diego's side?

69
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:52,106
I just want to know who her spy is.

70
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:56,402
I'm just curious, why are you
suddenly so interested?

71
00:03:56,945 --> 00:03:58,571
I mean, clearly, it's not an issue.

72
00:03:59,697 --> 00:04:01,407
Lily Cruz isn't coming out anyway.

73
00:04:02,367 --> 00:04:04,535
Besides, we have a wedding
to prepare. Right?

74
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:07,622
Yeah.

75
00:04:09,082 --> 00:04:10,500
Of course, Arnaldo.

76
00:04:11,834 --> 00:04:15,922
But, hon, I haven't forgotten
about our wedding.

77
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:19,467
I just want to help Emilia with this

78
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:23,054
for your future political career.

79
00:04:23,596 --> 00:04:26,766
I want to know that spy,

80
00:04:26,849 --> 00:04:30,812
so I can confirm
if Lily Cruz really is alive.

81
00:04:31,312 --> 00:04:33,690
Who knows? That spy could
just be stirring trouble.

82
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:38,194
That's all it is.

83
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:48,788
Here.

84
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,917
[Nimfa] Thank you, Mr. Marlon.

85
00:04:53,584 --> 00:04:55,420
I think you're forgetting something.

86
00:04:59,632 --> 00:05:00,800
Your number.

87
00:05:03,845 --> 00:05:05,722
Let me see that.

88
00:05:14,188 --> 00:05:15,565
I have to go.

89
00:05:16,899 --> 00:05:18,359
Nimfa, wait! Hang on.

90
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,570
-Hey!
-Stop it! Leave me alone!

91
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:23,281
What the hell is your problem?!

92
00:05:23,364 --> 00:05:25,074
-We were getting along well,
-Hey, Batch.

93
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:27,368
and then you slap me?! What did I do?!

94
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:30,413
-Hey, what's going on?!
-We were having fun!

95
00:05:30,496 --> 00:05:33,291
Marlon, you're drunk. Here, take a seat.

96
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:35,501
I drank a little, but I'm sober!

97
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:39,756
-Go on, sit down.
-That woman has a problem!

98
00:05:40,798 --> 00:05:42,091
[Diego] What happened?

99
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:43,051
-What happened?
-Ask her.

100
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:45,136
I didn't do anything wrong! Tell him!

101
00:05:45,803 --> 00:05:48,347
-What did you do to her?
-I didn't do anything!

102
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:51,684
Nimfa! Just a minute. Stay here. Nimfa!

103
00:05:53,311 --> 00:05:55,313
She's crazy!

104
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:58,232
Nimfa! Nimfa!

105
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:01,235
Nimfa, wait. Are you all right?

106
00:06:02,737 --> 00:06:05,031
I didn't think he'd do that to me.

107
00:06:05,615 --> 00:06:09,619
I was leaving, then he just
asked for my number.

108
00:06:11,913 --> 00:06:13,581
Thank goodness you arrived, Diego!

109
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:17,418
He would've harassed me
if it weren't for you.

110
00:06:18,002 --> 00:06:19,253
Marlon wouldn't do that, Nimfa.

111
00:06:20,421 --> 00:06:22,465
But, you should go home.
I'll take you, come on.

112
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:25,551
-No, Diego. No.
-Nimfa…

113
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:27,762
-Stay with me.
-Nimfa.

114
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:30,807
Please don't leave me.
Stay here! Stay with me.

115
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:34,727
-Nimfa, I think you're drunk.
-Stay with me. Stay with me.

116
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,145
Nimfa, stop!

117
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:40,191
What?! Don't you want me?
All the other guys do.

118
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:44,070
-Nimfa…
-They want this. They want me.

119
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:46,155
They want me. [crying]

120
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:49,158
Diego! Diego! Diego!

121
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:50,451
Nimfa, stop!

122
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:56,874
You have to understand, Nimfa,
that I'm in love with someone else.

123
00:06:58,417 --> 00:07:00,920
You have to stop.
You're only hurting yourself!

124
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:08,052
You bastard! You're a jerk! I hate you!

125
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:11,597
I did everything to make you mine!

126
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:13,683
I let her control me!

127
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:15,685
-Nimfa!
-I became a bad person!

128
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:17,645
-What?!
-I did everything!

129
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:18,813
What did you say?!

130
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,817
What do you mean, Nimfa? What do you mean?

131
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:26,446
What did you just say?

132
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:28,364
Diego.

133
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:34,537
Diego, I've loved you for so long.

134
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:35,997
What did you do, Nimfa?!

135
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:39,292
But, no matter how hard I tried,

136
00:07:39,375 --> 00:07:42,462
I couldn't take your mind off Lily.

137
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:48,468
And now, she's back…
You still want her, don't you?

138
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,804
How long are you going
to act like an idiot?

139
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:56,267
How long do you plan
on being so stupid?! How long?

140
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:59,228
-Nimfa, that's enough!
-Let me go! Let me go!

141
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:01,772
-Stop! Stop!
-Get off me!

142
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:03,024
I'm taking you home.

143
00:08:03,524 --> 00:08:05,318
No, let me go!

144
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:09,447
Nimfa, that's enough.
I'm taking you home. Let's go.

145
00:08:09,822 --> 00:08:12,325
That's enough, okay? Let's go.

146
00:08:13,117 --> 00:08:16,287
Don't touch me! Don't touch me.

147
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:19,832
[Nimfa crying]

148
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:27,632
Stop crying, we have to go.
Come on, let me take you home.

149
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:42,855
Go ahead. Be with her.

150
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:46,859
But, mark my words…
If you two end up together,

151
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:48,986
I'll make every second
of your life miserable!

152
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:52,532
[tense music playing]

153
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:55,326
Nimfa.

154
00:08:57,745 --> 00:08:58,871
Nimfa!

155
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:01,874
-Nimfa, are you okay?
-Nimfa, are you okay?

156
00:09:23,896 --> 00:09:25,898
[soft instrumental playing]

157
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,441
[moans]

158
00:09:36,284 --> 00:09:37,368
-Raul?
-Yeah?

159
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:42,623
My goodness. Why are you home so late?

160
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:45,501
You know what I just found out?

161
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:47,295
Lily Cruz is alive.

162
00:09:47,378 --> 00:09:49,338
And I expected you to at least support me,

163
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:50,840
but where were you again?

164
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:53,426
-I'm sorry.
-Are you cheating on me again?

165
00:09:53,509 --> 00:09:55,553
Did you go back to your old ways?

166
00:09:55,636 --> 00:09:56,846
What? Answer me.

167
00:09:56,929 --> 00:10:01,142
I'm not cheating on you.
Let's just sleep. Ouch!

168
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:02,852
What's happening to you?

169
00:10:02,935 --> 00:10:05,104
-That hurt.
-What's wrong?

170
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:08,649
Is that a stab wound or a gunshot?

171
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:10,401
Who did this to you?

172
00:10:10,484 --> 00:10:12,612
-This is nothing.
-Who did that?

173
00:10:13,112 --> 00:10:17,617
I had an encounter with one of my clients.

174
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:20,411
We had a misunderstanding. The
bastard didn't want to pay me.

175
00:10:20,911 --> 00:10:22,622
I went after him, and he opened fire.

176
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:25,333
But I settled everything.
We sent him to prison.

177
00:10:25,916 --> 00:10:27,752
That bastard had no idea who I was.

178
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,338
-[Raul grunts]
-I'm sorry, Raul. I'm sorry.

179
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:33,633
-This isn't serious.
-Wait. Let me call a doctor,

180
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:36,927
just to make sure everything's
going to be okay. Hold on, okay?

181
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:38,596
[Raul groans]

182
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:42,808
Hello? Doc.

183
00:10:52,151 --> 00:10:54,070
<i>Why did Nimfa mention Lily?</i>

184
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:58,574
[Camia] <i>Lily confirmed</i>
<i>that Emilia planted a spy</i>

185
00:10:58,658 --> 00:10:59,742
<i>in our camp.</i>

186
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:02,370
<i>And there's only one person I suspect.</i>

187
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:05,122
<i>-Is it Nimfa?</i>
<i>-I know she's your friend…</i>

188
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:08,751
<i>but I can't help</i>
<i>but feel suspicious of her.</i>

189
00:11:08,834 --> 00:11:11,337
<i>I caught her going through my things.</i>

190
00:11:11,796 --> 00:11:15,007
<i>She told me that she needs money</i>
<i>for her sick father.</i>

191
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:18,302
[tense music playing]

192
00:11:21,889 --> 00:11:23,182
-[phone rings]
-Wait, you go on ahead.

193
00:11:23,265 --> 00:11:24,683
I need to answer this call.

194
00:11:25,059 --> 00:11:26,394
[phone rings]

195
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:29,313
-Yes?
-Hello, Mister Fernan.

196
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:32,400
-How are you?
-I'm good.

197
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:34,485
[chuckles] <i>Oh, yeah, Diego.</i>

198
00:11:34,568 --> 00:11:37,405
I'm sorry I couldn't help out
with your campaign.

199
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:39,490
My brother asked me to help
out with the sugar cane harvest.

200
00:11:39,573 --> 00:11:41,492
<i>He doesn't have enough people to help him.</i>

201
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:43,577
Harvest?

202
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:46,664
Isn't that bad for your health?

203
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:50,751
Not at all! I still have
strong bones, you know.

204
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:53,504
Who told you I was sick?

205
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:55,548
<i>Why do you sound so concerned?</i>

206
00:11:55,881 --> 00:12:00,302
Uh… No reason, Mr. Fernan.
Take care over there.

207
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:01,887
Okay, then.

208
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:08,894
<i>Nimfa, what have you done?</i>

209
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:15,860
It's Nimfa?

210
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:18,529
My suspicions were right.

211
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:22,158
She watches my mother's every move

212
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:26,745
and reports all your plans
to Emilia and the Ardientes.

213
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:30,958
The Ardientes get wind of
all your plans because of Nimfa.

214
00:12:31,041 --> 00:12:34,420
Your friend's so sweet.
She deserves a loyalty award.

215
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:38,757
Ivy, I don't know how Nimfa
could do this to me, either.

216
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:44,305
They are evil. They try to buy
everyone with their money.

217
00:12:44,388 --> 00:12:47,266
They'll do everything to hold on
to their power.

218
00:12:47,349 --> 00:12:49,268
That's why we shouldn't allow them to win.

219
00:12:49,351 --> 00:12:50,352
You need to mislead Emilia.

220
00:12:50,436 --> 00:12:52,938
She can't discover your true identity.

221
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:55,232
And I will keep an eye on Nimfa.

222
00:12:57,860 --> 00:13:00,154
Diego, I want you to be careful.

223
00:13:00,237 --> 00:13:02,072
And thank you for all your help.

224
00:13:04,825 --> 00:13:06,410
Ivy, you need to be careful.

225
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:18,839
-You should go.
-Take care.

226
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:25,971
Thank you.

227
00:13:28,557 --> 00:13:30,518
-Emilia.
-Yes, Aunt Claire?

228
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:31,936
It's confirmed.

229
00:13:32,019 --> 00:13:34,605
This check didn't come from Ivy Aguas.

230
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:37,858
Who gave it then?

231
00:13:37,942 --> 00:13:40,486
From a small company based here
in Ardiente.

232
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:44,240
[screams]

233
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:46,450
Emilia, get it together.

234
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:52,665
I'm so sick of being patient
and following all their orders!

235
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:54,959
But this time around,
I'm gonna do it my way,

236
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:57,127
so I can end this damn charade!

237
00:13:57,211 --> 00:13:58,420
So, what are you going to do?

238
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:02,550
Emilia?

239
00:14:04,176 --> 00:14:05,928
Why the broken porcelain?

240
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:08,389
It's too early to throw things around.

241
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:09,682
Are you okay?

242
00:14:09,765 --> 00:14:10,766
Hi, Mamita.

243
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:12,893
It's a good thing you're here.

244
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:14,812
I was supposed to drop by your house.

245
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:18,482
I came here because I received
an invitation

246
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:21,944
from Senator Olivarez.
Let's go to his birthday party.

247
00:14:22,027 --> 00:14:25,197
We might be able to convince him
to endorse Arnaldo.

248
00:14:25,614 --> 00:14:27,408
No. I don't want to.

249
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:30,411
I can't concentrate because of Lily Cruz.

250
00:14:30,494 --> 00:14:32,454
That's why you have to keep your promise.

251
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:36,500
We're going to hunt Lily Cruz. Okay?

252
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:39,795
Sure.

253
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:45,175
<i>It's a good thing you're an idiot, Emilia.</i>

254
00:14:45,843 --> 00:14:48,762
<i>She's right in front of you, moron.</i>

255
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:51,390
Thank you, Ivy.

256
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:57,062
[crowd murmuring]

257
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:59,773
[woman] Lily Cruz?
That's Camia Cruz's daughter.

258
00:14:59,857 --> 00:15:01,692
The woman going against the Ardientes.

259
00:15:01,775 --> 00:15:04,528
-I thought she was dead?
-She's still alive.

260
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:08,365
[woman 1] <i>Haven't you heard?</i>
<i>Emilia's nabbing all the women</i>

261
00:15:08,449 --> 00:15:09,992
<i>who are the same age as Lily Cruz.</i>

262
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:18,375
-Help! Help us!
-Somebody help us!

263
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:20,753
What will you do to them?
Where are you taking them?

264
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:25,215
Ivy, relax. You know,
you should take a chill pill.

265
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:28,594
I won't do anything today
that you won't like.

266
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:31,013
[ominous music playing]

267
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:37,561
-Come with us.
-Where are you taking us?

268
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,188
-Where are you taking us?
-Please, no…

269
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:40,481
Where are you taking us?

270
00:15:40,564 --> 00:15:41,815
Get in.

271
00:15:49,114 --> 00:15:50,866
-Come with us.
-Who are you?

272
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:54,119
Who are you? Let me go, mister!

273
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:57,748
-Mister! Let go of me!
-Hey!

274
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:02,503
[man] <i>What will Emilia do to them?</i>

275
00:16:02,878 --> 00:16:07,132
Let's just pray that Emilia
doesn't go completely insane.

276
00:16:07,549 --> 00:16:09,051
She's acting like she's possessed.

277
00:16:09,885 --> 00:16:11,512
-That's right.
-You need to be careful, okay?

278
00:16:11,595 --> 00:16:14,223
-And you?
-Emilia's pure evil.

279
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:15,349
Right.

280
00:16:24,733 --> 00:16:25,901
[goon] Stay there!

281
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:31,699
-Stay there!
-[women crying]

282
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:41,875
-Is that all of them?
-From two communities, ma'am.

283
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:43,460
We haven't gone to the town proper yet.

284
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:46,005
Emilia, why did you have
to take them here?

285
00:16:46,422 --> 00:16:47,756
What are you going to do with them?

286
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,508
Ivy, just watch.

287
00:16:52,177 --> 00:16:53,220
Emilia…

288
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:57,141
Why are you all crying?
I haven't done anything yet.

289
00:16:57,725 --> 00:16:58,809
Well?

290
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:00,644
Stop crying!

291
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:07,484
Oh, girls, it's like
you don't know me at all.

292
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:11,613
I only brought you here because
I wanted us to chat a little.

293
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:13,532
So, how are you, friends?

294
00:17:13,615 --> 00:17:17,244
Mrs. Emilia, why did you take us here?

295
00:17:19,204 --> 00:17:22,458
What do you think?
Why would I bring you here?

296
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,253
Because you're looking for
Lily Cruz, Camia's daughter.

297
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:30,090
You're right. And why do
you think I'm looking for her?

298
00:17:30,799 --> 00:17:33,802
Because you're afraid she might
file charges against you,

299
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:35,304
like what Camia did.

300
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:37,431
-Emilia, stop it?
-What did you say?!

301
00:17:37,514 --> 00:17:39,224
-Emilia!
-What did you say?! Tell me!

302
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:40,851
Do I look afraid?!

303
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:42,603
-Emi--
-Stay there!

304
00:17:44,396 --> 00:17:45,939
Stop it, please.

305
00:17:47,816 --> 00:17:48,776
Next.

306
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:52,279
What's your name?

307
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,782
Evangeline Macaspac, ma'am.

308
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:59,286
How would I know
if you're telling the truth?

309
00:17:59,369 --> 00:18:04,708
Or if that's just your alias?
What if you're Lily Cruz?

310
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:09,963
Mrs. Emilia, I'm not Lily Cruz.

311
00:18:10,672 --> 00:18:13,050
I'm the daughter of Mando
and Linda Macaspac.

312
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:17,179
I'm a public school teacher.
I'm not Lily Cruz.

313
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:21,350
You talk too much! Stay back! Go!

314
00:18:22,684 --> 00:18:27,481
You're all too loud!
Shut up! Come here. Now!

315
00:18:28,398 --> 00:18:30,692
[women crying]

316
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:33,612
[Emilia] Stop crying.
You! What's your name?

317
00:18:35,697 --> 00:18:37,533
Everyone, even though the senator's party

318
00:18:37,616 --> 00:18:39,159
is helping us with the campaign,

319
00:18:39,243 --> 00:18:42,162
I still want us to have
our own source of funds.

320
00:18:42,538 --> 00:18:46,542
Let's organize dance and game festivals…

321
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:48,794
as well as weekend markets.

322
00:18:48,877 --> 00:18:51,088
If you have other suggestions,
just tell Nimfa.

323
00:18:51,171 --> 00:18:53,382
Nimfa. You'll be my assistant from now on.

324
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:57,719
What? All right. I would love to.

325
00:19:00,556 --> 00:19:02,558
-Lucky you, Nimfa.
-[laughs]

326
00:19:02,641 --> 00:19:05,144
Well, since you're his assistant now,

327
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:07,521
help me prepare some snacks for them.

328
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:08,814
-Yes, ma'am.
-Pandoy.

329
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:12,317
[tense music playing]

330
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:18,699
Batch. What was that?
You sided with her last night,

331
00:19:18,782 --> 00:19:20,367
and now, you even made her your assistant?

332
00:19:20,784 --> 00:19:22,244
I know you did nothing wrong, Batch.

333
00:19:22,578 --> 00:19:25,789
I'm just doing this
to avoid any conflict here.

334
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:27,916
-That's just it.
-All right then.

335
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,586
[phone rings]

336
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:34,548
I'll just take this.

337
00:19:36,633 --> 00:19:39,303
-Hello, Ivy.
-Are you at the headquarters?

338
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:40,888
Yes, why?

339
00:19:42,097 --> 00:19:44,641
Emilia's looking for Lily Cruz.

340
00:19:44,725 --> 00:19:47,311
She's scouring all of Ardiente

341
00:19:47,394 --> 00:19:49,605
and abducting every woman of Lily's age.

342
00:19:52,774 --> 00:19:53,984
-[Emilia] Next!
-She's going to…

343
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:55,235
your headquarters next.

344
00:19:55,861 --> 00:19:57,529
Ivy, get out of there. It's too dangerous.

345
00:19:57,613 --> 00:19:59,031
-<i>I can't do that.</i>
-[Emilia] <i>Idiots!</i>

346
00:19:59,114 --> 00:20:00,490
-[Emilia] What's your name?
-I need to stay here…

347
00:20:00,574 --> 00:20:02,534
-to know about Emilia's plans.
-[Emilia] What?!

348
00:20:02,618 --> 00:20:04,119
Diego, I just have one favor to ask.

349
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:07,456
Please… keep my mother safe.

350
00:20:08,248 --> 00:20:09,791
Don't worry, I'll take care of her.

351
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:13,045
[Emilia] Rose Ann? Get over there!

352
00:20:24,306 --> 00:20:25,265
Diego.

353
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:27,017
What's wrong?

354
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:34,650
[Emilia] You! Come here. What's your name?

355
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:36,693
-Susanna.
-Next!

356
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:39,696
-Emilia, stop it. Enough.
-Please stop!

357
00:20:40,155 --> 00:20:41,531
You, what's your name?

358
00:20:43,158 --> 00:20:44,993
You idiot! Get lost.

359
00:20:45,661 --> 00:20:48,497
-Come here!
-You! What's your name?

360
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:52,000
[tense music playing]

361
00:20:58,465 --> 00:20:59,466
Mm.

362
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:04,346
Arnaldo, where's your mother?
I need to talk to her.

363
00:21:05,097 --> 00:21:11,144
Mom and Ivy went hunting.
They're hunting Lily Cruz.

364
00:21:11,478 --> 00:21:13,689
But I'm going to stop them
before things get worse.

365
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:18,527
No, no, no. I think your mom
is right this time.

366
00:21:19,945 --> 00:21:24,491
Lily Cruz's resurgence will only
be like opening Pandora's box.

367
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:29,329
Dead witnesses, closed cases,
and people I had to get rid of

368
00:21:29,413 --> 00:21:31,581
because they were in the way of our plans.

369
00:21:32,749 --> 00:21:34,126
It's best that we deal

370
00:21:34,209 --> 00:21:37,754
with this Lily Cruz fiasco
as soon as possible.

371
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:42,342
There!

372
00:21:42,426 --> 00:21:45,262
Since you didn't get anything
from them, let them go.

373
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:48,557
Too soon, Ivy. Too soon.

374
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:52,436
And you.

375
00:21:54,187 --> 00:21:58,108
I overlooked your failure to catch Jaguar.

376
00:21:58,775 --> 00:22:01,862
And now you can't even
help your crazy wife.

377
00:22:02,612 --> 00:22:05,574
And all the while I thought
you rekindled your love

378
00:22:05,657 --> 00:22:06,783
for each other?

379
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:10,370
Or… are you just saying you love your wife

380
00:22:10,454 --> 00:22:12,914
whenever it's convenient?

381
00:22:14,791 --> 00:22:16,626
I really do love my wife, Papa.

382
00:22:17,294 --> 00:22:20,756
But a problem came up
with the business I'm running.

383
00:22:20,839 --> 00:22:23,508
I'm still taking care of it. I'm sorry.

384
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:26,011
I'm not your wife,

385
00:22:26,094 --> 00:22:29,264
but I can smell
your mistress from miles away.

386
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:34,436
Raul, I know you're hiding something.

387
00:22:35,979 --> 00:22:39,775
Don't wait for me to find out,
or you'll be sorry.

388
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:42,235
You and my daughter are made
for each other.

389
00:22:42,694 --> 00:22:44,571
You're both sloppy.

390
00:22:59,002 --> 00:23:01,588
Emilia, aren't you getting tired of this?

391
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:04,966
You're scaring
all these women for nothing!

392
00:23:05,050 --> 00:23:06,927
-I know!
-Stop this nonsense!

393
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:09,638
I'm going to stop interrogating, okay?

394
00:23:09,721 --> 00:23:11,389
But I can't leave a stone unturned.

395
00:23:11,473 --> 00:23:15,811
Oh, there you go!
Good afternoon, Camia Cruz!

396
00:23:15,894 --> 00:23:17,354
I am looking for…

397
00:23:17,437 --> 00:23:21,900
You're going to kidnap the
women here to find Lily Cruz.

398
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:26,863
Yes, Emilia. I know all
about your dirty games.

399
00:23:27,155 --> 00:23:29,616
What you're doing is against human rights!

400
00:23:29,699 --> 00:23:33,370
But whatever you do,
you'll never find Lily here!

401
00:23:34,329 --> 00:23:36,665
You know, I really enjoy
talking to this woman.

402
00:23:36,748 --> 00:23:38,375
She's so feisty!

403
00:23:38,458 --> 00:23:39,835
Maybe your daughter is just like you.

404
00:23:39,918 --> 00:23:42,838
But why isn't she here? Is she scared?

405
00:23:43,797 --> 00:23:47,676
It doesn't matter. Um, Lily! Yoo-hoo!

406
00:23:48,051 --> 00:23:52,722
Yoo-hoo! Lily, I'm here! Lily, I'm here!

407
00:23:52,806 --> 00:23:54,558
-Emilia…
-I'm going to get you!

408
00:23:54,641 --> 00:23:57,102
This is frustrating.
Why won't you come out?

409
00:23:57,185 --> 00:23:59,521
Okay, if you don't want to come out…

410
00:23:59,604 --> 00:24:01,231
just watch this.

411
00:24:01,314 --> 00:24:04,276
Get some popcorn, and enjoy the movie.

412
00:24:04,359 --> 00:24:06,361
Boys! Now.

413
00:24:06,444 --> 00:24:07,529
-Wait!
-Emilia!

414
00:24:07,612 --> 00:24:08,530
[Camia] Hey!

415
00:24:08,613 --> 00:24:12,242
-Emilia! You're going crazy!
-Am I, Camia?

416
00:24:12,576 --> 00:24:14,703
Because as I understand it,

417
00:24:14,786 --> 00:24:19,082
if a daughter sees her mother in danger,

418
00:24:19,541 --> 00:24:21,376
she'll come out and save her, right?

419
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:24,629
So, I assume Lily will do the same.

420
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:26,256
Take her. Now.

421
00:24:26,339 --> 00:24:28,383
-Emilia, please.
-You can't take Aunt Camia!

422
00:24:28,884 --> 00:24:29,885
Ah.

423
00:24:30,385 --> 00:24:33,597
Wait, did I just hear
you say "Aunt," Diego?

424
00:24:34,764 --> 00:24:36,766
Diego! I turn away for a second, and now…

425
00:24:36,850 --> 00:24:39,060
you're calling this woman
like she's a blood relative?

426
00:24:39,769 --> 00:24:44,900
You ungrateful piece of crap.
Unbelievable. Get them!

427
00:24:44,983 --> 00:24:47,652
-Brace yourselves!
-Try us! Try us!

428
00:24:47,736 --> 00:24:48,945
[clamoring]

429
00:24:49,029 --> 00:24:52,490
-Emilia, please stop this!
-[Camia] Hold on. Wait!

430
00:24:53,783 --> 00:24:56,203
Emilia! Fine, Emilia.

431
00:24:56,703 --> 00:24:59,789
Because I don't want
these people to get hurt,

432
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:01,082
I'll come with you.

433
00:25:01,166 --> 00:25:04,377
But promise me that nothing bad
will happen to me,

434
00:25:04,461 --> 00:25:05,795
because if you don't,

435
00:25:05,879 --> 00:25:09,549
all these people are witnesses
to your barbarity towards me!

436
00:25:10,425 --> 00:25:14,262
Okay, okay. Quit whining.
Come on. Let's go.

437
00:25:14,346 --> 00:25:15,347
Emilia.

438
00:25:16,514 --> 00:25:18,308
-Ma'am Camia!
-I'm gonna follow you.

439
00:25:18,391 --> 00:25:19,684
Ma'am Camia.

440
00:25:19,768 --> 00:25:22,145
[crowd murmuring]

441
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:23,313
[quietly] Mom.

442
00:25:24,147 --> 00:25:28,485
[tense music playing]

443
00:25:51,258 --> 00:25:54,010
Bodyguards, follow them! Nanny, Uncle.

444
00:25:54,094 --> 00:25:55,929
-Wait.
-We're going after them.

445
00:25:56,012 --> 00:25:58,139
[Loring] What? Diego!

446
00:25:58,223 --> 00:25:59,474
Marlon, take charge here!

447
00:25:59,557 --> 00:26:01,184
-I'll take care of this.
-I can do this.

448
00:26:01,810 --> 00:26:02,602
-Take care, all right?
-Diego.

449
00:26:02,686 --> 00:26:03,645
-Take care, Diego.
-Yes, take care.

450
00:26:03,728 --> 00:26:07,232
Take care, Batch, okay? Take care.

451
00:26:12,988 --> 00:26:16,449
Why is Emilia looking for Lily Cruz here?

452
00:26:16,533 --> 00:26:19,494
And why bother? She's been dead for years!

453
00:26:20,328 --> 00:26:23,915
Ma'am Camia's problems never seem to end!

454
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:25,667
Now, even Diego's involved.

455
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:28,003
I just hope this all ends soon.

456
00:26:28,086 --> 00:26:31,631
Miss Loring, Mister Pandoy… Lily is alive!

457
00:26:31,715 --> 00:26:32,882
And she's here somewhere.

458
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:34,259
-What?!
-What?!

459
00:26:34,884 --> 00:26:36,553
What are you talking about?

460
00:26:37,971 --> 00:26:40,223
I didn't tell Mrs. Emilia anything!

461
00:26:41,808 --> 00:26:43,268
What about Emilia?

462
00:26:43,351 --> 00:26:44,936
[tense music playing]

463
00:26:45,020 --> 00:26:46,021
Uh.

464
00:26:48,898 --> 00:26:50,400
Oh. What are you staring at?!

465
00:26:58,992 --> 00:27:00,285
-Papa!
-Yes?

466
00:27:00,368 --> 00:27:03,538
Arnaldo! Look who we have here.

467
00:27:04,205 --> 00:27:06,249
-What?
-Hon.

468
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:07,334
Hon.

469
00:27:11,921 --> 00:27:13,631
Whoa! [chuckles]

470
00:27:14,257 --> 00:27:15,258
Wow!

471
00:27:16,176 --> 00:27:19,804
Now, this is a surprise!

472
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:23,099
Miss Camia Cruz…

473
00:27:23,183 --> 00:27:25,769
To what do we owe this pleasure?

474
00:27:25,852 --> 00:27:29,022
[tense music playing]

475
00:28:02,555 --> 00:28:03,932
[guards] You aren't allowed in here.

476
00:28:04,557 --> 00:28:06,184
Oh, I get it!

477
00:28:07,185 --> 00:28:10,480
Emilia, you're using Miss Camia Cruz

478
00:28:10,563 --> 00:28:14,567
to lure Lily Cruz into the lion's den.

479
00:28:15,860 --> 00:28:17,195
Yes, Papa.

480
00:28:18,738 --> 00:28:19,906
Very well, then.

481
00:28:19,989 --> 00:28:21,658
Let me get the happy place ready.

482
00:28:21,741 --> 00:28:22,659
Wait!

483
00:28:24,828 --> 00:28:26,037
Emilia, have you forgotten

484
00:28:26,121 --> 00:28:28,164
about the promise you made to the people.

485
00:28:28,248 --> 00:28:32,335
You swore you wouldn't
lay a hand on Camia Cruz.

486
00:28:32,919 --> 00:28:38,299
If you do, it'll hurt Arnaldo's campaign!

487
00:28:39,509 --> 00:28:42,887
If I were you, I'd keep your promise.

488
00:28:44,514 --> 00:28:47,434
You know, Ivy, sometimes
you can really be silly.

489
00:28:48,268 --> 00:28:52,313
You still don't know the family
you're marrying into.

490
00:28:52,605 --> 00:28:55,024
You don't know how ruthless we can be!

491
00:29:00,989 --> 00:29:04,033
-No, let me go!
-You're not allowed in here.

492
00:29:07,579 --> 00:29:09,247
[action music playing]

493
00:29:20,216 --> 00:29:21,176
Hold them here!

494
00:29:24,387 --> 00:29:25,430
Take her!

495
00:29:29,058 --> 00:29:31,186
-Don't touch me.
-[Diego] Let her go!

496
00:29:33,313 --> 00:29:35,315
[suspenseful music playing]

497
00:30:00,965 --> 00:30:03,843
[suspenseful music playing]

498
00:30:33,206 --> 00:30:35,041
I'm here to talk to you.

499
00:30:36,459 --> 00:30:40,547
So let's keep things civil.
Put down your guns.

500
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:45,385
Put your guns down.
Let's talk about this properly!

501
00:30:53,601 --> 00:30:55,895
Put your guns down. Now!

502
00:31:01,901 --> 00:31:03,027
Emilia.

503
00:31:03,987 --> 00:31:05,113
Put it down.

504
00:31:08,408 --> 00:31:11,286
Arnaldo, put the gun down.

505
00:31:12,412 --> 00:31:13,663
Put it down.

506
00:31:35,101 --> 00:31:40,398
I guess now that we put the guns away…

507
00:31:41,357 --> 00:31:44,777
it's your turn to fulfill your promise.

508
00:31:47,488 --> 00:31:48,531
Where's your daughter?

509
00:31:49,449 --> 00:31:52,368
How'd you find out
my daughter's still alive?

510
00:31:53,119 --> 00:31:55,246
It doesn't matter how I found out.

511
00:31:55,705 --> 00:31:58,917
Answer my question.
Is Lily alive?! Where is she?!

512
00:31:59,292 --> 00:32:02,128
Yes! Lily is alive!

513
00:32:02,420 --> 00:32:04,130
That's what you want to hear, right?!

514
00:32:04,213 --> 00:32:05,840
My daughter is alive!

515
00:32:09,677 --> 00:32:11,721
[suspenseful music playing]

516
00:32:14,557 --> 00:32:17,393
Well, if your daughter's alive,
where is she? Bring her to us.

517
00:32:17,685 --> 00:32:20,939
Is she helping you with Diego's campaign?

518
00:32:21,731 --> 00:32:24,484
Will she resurface?
Is she going to press charges?

519
00:32:24,567 --> 00:32:27,195
And will you admit you had
my daughter killed

520
00:32:27,278 --> 00:32:29,197
just like what you tried to do to me?

521
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:31,366
Will she resurface just as you did?

522
00:32:37,413 --> 00:32:41,376
Okay. You know what? We don't need this.

523
00:32:42,043 --> 00:32:44,128
We'll only have a harder time
with the election.

524
00:32:45,546 --> 00:32:48,800
No, Arnaldo. I can eliminate the threat.

525
00:32:49,425 --> 00:32:50,969
Are you trying to scare me, Emilia?

526
00:32:53,888 --> 00:32:56,766
Camia. You're on our turf.

527
00:32:57,141 --> 00:33:00,019
And I'm the one who calls the shots here.

528
00:33:00,520 --> 00:33:03,022
And if you don't stick
to our agreement, Camia…

529
00:33:03,106 --> 00:33:05,358
You heard about those women
I nabbed, right?

530
00:33:05,692 --> 00:33:08,444
I'll kill them all, one by one.

531
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:15,118
Lily will not resurface.

532
00:33:16,411 --> 00:33:18,121
I promise you that.

533
00:33:18,830 --> 00:33:19,998
[Julio] Wait a minute.

534
00:33:21,833 --> 00:33:26,587
How can we be sure that you're not lying?

535
00:33:28,047 --> 00:33:31,843
If I don't follow the deal
you set, what will you do to me?

536
00:33:32,969 --> 00:33:34,387
You'll have me killed?

537
00:33:35,304 --> 00:33:38,307
You're going to stain your name
with me and my daughter's blood?

538
00:33:38,808 --> 00:33:41,644
[scoffs] And during
election season, no less!

539
00:33:42,729 --> 00:33:46,691
Not even the fortune of this
Ivy Aguas can save you.

540
00:33:47,567 --> 00:33:50,111
Your family will be ruined, and
there's no way you'll recover.

541
00:34:04,584 --> 00:34:08,004
Aunt Camia, how are you? Are you okay?

542
00:34:10,006 --> 00:34:15,136
Diego, the Ardientes already
know that Lily is still alive.

543
00:34:16,929 --> 00:34:20,808
I think… I think I need
to talk to my daughter.

544
00:34:44,373 --> 00:34:45,833
WE NEED TO TALK. LET'S MEET.

545
00:34:48,419 --> 00:34:51,047
Hon, I need to go.

546
00:34:51,631 --> 00:34:52,882
But why?

547
00:34:52,965 --> 00:34:54,967
If you need to rest, you can stay here.

548
00:34:55,510 --> 00:34:57,386
I can rest better at home.

549
00:34:58,387 --> 00:35:00,389
Okay, but I'll have the driver
take you home.

550
00:35:01,182 --> 00:35:02,892
That won't be necessary, hon.

551
00:35:03,267 --> 00:35:04,727
I'll just see you tomorrow, okay?

552
00:35:05,311 --> 00:35:07,271
-Emilia, good night.
-Good night.

553
00:35:07,355 --> 00:35:08,606
Congressman.

554
00:35:10,358 --> 00:35:12,276
-Good night.
-Good night.

555
00:35:13,319 --> 00:35:15,196
Good night, hon. I love you.

556
00:35:15,905 --> 00:35:17,073
[Arnaldo] I love you too.

557
00:35:21,577 --> 00:35:22,537
See you tomorrow.

558
00:35:22,620 --> 00:35:25,206
Good night. See you tomorrow.
I'll just see her out.

559
00:35:25,289 --> 00:35:28,126
-Okay.
-You're so sweet! Bye!

560
00:35:31,712 --> 00:35:33,422
She's sweet tonight.

561
00:35:35,842 --> 00:35:37,301
Romeo and Juliet!

562
00:35:37,385 --> 00:35:38,928
[chuckles]

563
00:35:39,512 --> 00:35:40,513
Ah!

564
00:35:41,639 --> 00:35:44,433
I think I'm going to call it a night too.

565
00:35:44,851 --> 00:35:47,061
Good night, earthlings!

566
00:35:47,728 --> 00:35:52,817
Tomorrow's another day to catch
the traitors of this family.

567
00:35:54,610 --> 00:35:57,864
I believe my daughter's
got all the bases covered?

568
00:35:58,990 --> 00:36:01,200
Yes, Papa. You just wait and see.

569
00:36:02,869 --> 00:36:03,995
Very good.

570
00:36:04,078 --> 00:36:05,955
-Good night, Papa.
-Good night.

571
00:36:06,247 --> 00:36:08,666
-Rest well.
-And you too.

572
00:36:09,792 --> 00:36:10,668
[grunts]

573
00:36:12,128 --> 00:36:15,548
[melancholic music playing]

574
00:36:19,552 --> 00:36:22,638
[ominous music playing]

575
00:36:24,891 --> 00:36:25,933
[phone ringing]

576
00:36:27,727 --> 00:36:28,644
Hello?

577
00:36:29,729 --> 00:36:32,773
I'm sure about this,
Ma'am Emilia. Lily's coming.

578
00:36:33,232 --> 00:36:35,526
And I'll find out just who she is.

579
00:36:35,985 --> 00:36:39,113
Take a video, and send it
to me immediately.

580
00:36:39,572 --> 00:36:42,450
If you pull that off, you're free to go.

581
00:36:42,992 --> 00:36:44,911
<i>And I'll send the remaining</i>
<i>balance to you,</i>

582
00:36:44,994 --> 00:36:46,120
<i>the house and lot as well.</i>

583
00:36:47,455 --> 00:36:48,497
Good job.

584
00:36:50,041 --> 00:36:52,376
[quietly] Thank you. Thank you, ma'am.

585
00:36:52,877 --> 00:36:54,587
Just a little bit more,

586
00:36:54,670 --> 00:36:56,881
and I can finally make
my dreams come true.

587
00:36:59,050 --> 00:36:59,926
Bye-bye.

588
00:37:07,016 --> 00:37:10,561
[suspenseful music playing]

589
00:37:43,636 --> 00:37:44,720
[gasps]

590
00:37:44,804 --> 00:37:48,557
[suspenseful music playing]

591
00:37:54,355 --> 00:37:55,356
[gasps]

592
00:38:06,409 --> 00:38:09,870
[muffled shriek]

593
00:38:11,247 --> 00:38:12,540
[no audible dialogue]

594
00:38:14,417 --> 00:38:18,546
Mom. I'm sorry that I had
to point a gun at you earlier.

595
00:38:20,172 --> 00:38:22,675
It's all right, Lily. I understand why.

596
00:38:32,310 --> 00:38:33,894
The survey results are about to come out.

597
00:38:33,978 --> 00:38:35,771
We need to gain the public's sympathy.

598
00:38:35,855 --> 00:38:39,650
That's why I took it upon myself
to find you an electoral party.

599
00:38:39,734 --> 00:38:40,776
Here.

600
00:38:44,488 --> 00:38:45,823
It's tonight.

601
00:38:46,782 --> 00:38:48,993
It's Senator Olivares' birthday.

602
00:38:50,494 --> 00:38:52,705
He's Senator Magno's rival.

603
00:38:54,373 --> 00:38:56,000
Well, let me guess…

604
00:38:56,792 --> 00:38:59,837
-You want me to charm this man.
-No.

605
00:39:00,463 --> 00:39:02,006
I want something else to happen.

606
00:39:02,882 --> 00:39:07,553
I want them to bend
over backward to make you

607
00:39:07,636 --> 00:39:08,804
a part of their party.

608
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:10,806
It's different, right?

609
00:39:10,890 --> 00:39:12,808
[pensive music playing]

610
00:39:16,520 --> 00:39:17,855
Want some, hon?

611
00:39:17,938 --> 00:39:19,315
Sure. Thank you.

612
00:39:24,779 --> 00:39:29,408
Senator Carlito Olivares' birthday…

613
00:39:29,492 --> 00:39:31,077
For Arnaldo?

614
00:39:32,536 --> 00:39:33,871
No, thanks. [scoffs]

615
00:39:34,330 --> 00:39:38,626
Ever since he became active
in human rights causes,

616
00:39:39,210 --> 00:39:41,629
I stopped associating with him.

617
00:39:42,838 --> 00:39:44,256
But, Papa, you and his father

618
00:39:44,340 --> 00:39:45,674
used to belong to the same party.

619
00:39:45,758 --> 00:39:49,553
And I remember having breakfast
with his dad when I was young.

620
00:39:50,179 --> 00:39:55,851
His dad, yes. But Carlito? He's two-faced.

621
00:39:55,935 --> 00:39:59,480
I don't want anything
to do with him, with his party,

622
00:39:59,563 --> 00:40:02,066
whether political or otherwise.

623
00:40:02,733 --> 00:40:06,153
Fine. I just thought it could help Arnaldo

624
00:40:06,237 --> 00:40:08,781
if we attended as a complete family.

625
00:40:10,741 --> 00:40:12,326
I'll think about it.

626
00:40:13,828 --> 00:40:15,246
Anyway, how about you?

627
00:40:15,663 --> 00:40:17,540
Have you fixed all your problems?

628
00:40:17,623 --> 00:40:22,294
Is that why you're looking for
another endeavor to screw up?

629
00:40:22,795 --> 00:40:24,839
I know Camia and Diego.

630
00:40:26,048 --> 00:40:29,718
Knowing them, they're willing
to sacrifice their own agenda

631
00:40:29,802 --> 00:40:31,846
for everyone's safety, Papa.

632
00:40:32,304 --> 00:40:35,433
So, I believe they won't reveal Lily Cruz.

633
00:40:35,766 --> 00:40:38,519
Well, not for now or in the near future.

634
00:40:40,896 --> 00:40:41,939
I see.

635
00:40:42,273 --> 00:40:44,817
How could you do this to us, Nimfa?

636
00:40:46,277 --> 00:40:48,028
We were good to you!

637
00:40:48,946 --> 00:40:51,824
How could you rat us out to Emilia?

638
00:40:52,658 --> 00:40:54,869
Why did you let her use you?!

639
00:40:59,582 --> 00:41:01,667
Because I'm sick of this life!

640
00:41:03,043 --> 00:41:04,211
Why?

641
00:41:04,295 --> 00:41:06,797
Can you give me what she promised?

642
00:41:07,631 --> 00:41:10,134
You're only relying on your backer.

643
00:41:10,676 --> 00:41:14,889
Diego is your friend.
You threw all that away.

644
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:19,435
For what?! For what, Nimfa?!

645
00:41:19,518 --> 00:41:20,853
It's none of your business!

646
00:41:22,605 --> 00:41:24,815
Why? Do you have any proof?

647
00:41:26,901 --> 00:41:28,611
Just let me go.

648
00:41:29,236 --> 00:41:31,238
There's no point to this!

649
00:41:31,989 --> 00:41:34,158
I need to get my prize.

650
00:41:35,951 --> 00:41:37,411
-Give it to me!
-Let go!

651
00:41:37,495 --> 00:41:38,871
-Give it to me!
-Let go of me!

652
00:41:38,954 --> 00:41:40,206
-I said give it to me!
-Auntie.

653
00:41:43,334 --> 00:41:45,836
MA'AM E, I HEARD CAMIA
IS GOING TO MEET UP WITH LILY.

654
00:41:49,381 --> 00:41:50,549
KEEP A CLOSE EYE ON CAMIA,

655
00:41:50,633 --> 00:41:52,176
-AND TAKE A VIDEO OF THEM BOTH.
-OKAY, MA'AM E.

656
00:41:54,970 --> 00:41:56,138
How dare you?!

657
00:41:56,222 --> 00:41:57,723
[Nimfa grunting]

658
00:41:57,806 --> 00:41:59,642
-Aunt Camia!
-Let go of me!

659
00:41:59,725 --> 00:42:00,893
Auntie! Auntie!

660
00:42:00,976 --> 00:42:03,729
How dare you?! You idiot! You liar!

661
00:42:04,313 --> 00:42:05,564
[sobs]

662
00:42:05,648 --> 00:42:08,234
Diego. Diego. Diego.

663
00:42:10,402 --> 00:42:12,530
-Diego!
-Nimfa, how could you do this?

664
00:42:13,614 --> 00:42:15,157
-Diego.
-What were you thinking?

665
00:42:15,241 --> 00:42:17,576
-Diego, forgive…
-Why did you do that?!

666
00:42:20,621 --> 00:42:23,457
Because I want to be like Ivy Aguas.

667
00:42:27,586 --> 00:42:30,214
Emilia promised to give me a better life.

668
00:42:31,840 --> 00:42:36,011
I was blinded by it because
I'm sick of being so poor!

669
00:42:37,596 --> 00:42:40,849
I want to become rich, to have
a car and my own business.

670
00:42:41,517 --> 00:42:43,602
Haven't you realized
that they're just using you?

671
00:42:44,019 --> 00:42:46,480
There are other ways
to achieve your dreams.

672
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:50,317
You know Emilia and her family
are murderers and liars!

673
00:42:51,235 --> 00:42:54,697
Diego, Emilia promised me
you'd be mine after all this.

674
00:42:54,780 --> 00:42:56,323
Well, she lied to you!

675
00:42:56,907 --> 00:43:01,745
I did all this hoping
I could make you love me, Diego!

676
00:43:04,582 --> 00:43:08,919
But you only have eyes for Ivy… for Lily.

677
00:43:12,339 --> 00:43:14,091
[Nimfa crying]

678
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:24,184
Black diamond?

679
00:43:25,227 --> 00:43:27,187
Wait, I have to take off my earrings.

680
00:43:27,271 --> 00:43:28,897
-It doesn't match the necklace.
-Mm-hm.

681
00:43:28,981 --> 00:43:30,649
Thank you, but what is this for?

682
00:43:30,983 --> 00:43:36,697
I just want to thank you
for helping me find Lily Cruz.

683
00:43:37,740 --> 00:43:39,617
You know, I just appreciate your effort.

684
00:43:40,868 --> 00:43:43,537
It's nothing. But, thank you.
It's beautiful.

685
00:43:43,621 --> 00:43:44,872
You're welcome.

686
00:43:44,955 --> 00:43:48,083
So, shall I see you at Senator
Olivares' party later?

687
00:43:48,500 --> 00:43:51,462
Yes, of course. I'll see
you later. I have to go.

688
00:43:51,545 --> 00:43:54,131
Wait, Ivy. I'm just curious.

689
00:43:54,715 --> 00:43:57,551
How did you get an invite to the party?

690
00:43:58,385 --> 00:44:01,472
It's simple. I am Ivy Aguas.

691
00:44:02,598 --> 00:44:06,060
I own the top company here in
the country. So, I'm in demand.

692
00:44:07,519 --> 00:44:08,646
Hmm.

693
00:44:09,063 --> 00:44:14,026
That's why you even got Arnaldo
and our whole family invited.

694
00:44:14,568 --> 00:44:17,404
But, do you even think
it's worth our attendance?

695
00:44:17,946 --> 00:44:19,198
[scoffs]

696
00:44:19,281 --> 00:44:21,408
I didn't do it for nothing.

697
00:44:21,492 --> 00:44:25,037
Let's just say we're hitting
two birds with one stone.

698
00:44:25,120 --> 00:44:28,540
And, yes, if we secure
Senator Olivares' endorsement

699
00:44:28,624 --> 00:44:32,336
for Arnaldo's campaign then
it means, it's all worth it.

700
00:44:35,005 --> 00:44:36,256
What about you, Emilia?

701
00:44:36,340 --> 00:44:38,550
It seems like you didn't get an invite.

702
00:44:38,967 --> 00:44:40,094
Hmm?

703
00:44:40,177 --> 00:44:42,930
Me? What are you saying, Ivy?

704
00:44:43,013 --> 00:44:46,225
I'm Emilia Ardiente,
the queen of Ardiente.

705
00:44:46,642 --> 00:44:48,769
Of course, I have an invite! Come on.

706
00:44:49,186 --> 00:44:53,482
Oh, right. You're in demand too.
You want to have this?

707
00:44:55,484 --> 00:44:57,986
Aww. We're exchanging gifts now?

708
00:44:58,070 --> 00:45:00,239
-Aww. Thank you.
-Why not?

709
00:45:00,697 --> 00:45:02,616
-You're welcome.
-[giggles]

710
00:45:03,325 --> 00:45:05,285
So sweet of my daughter-in-law.

711
00:45:06,995 --> 00:45:08,789
And when Arnaldo and I get married,

712
00:45:08,872 --> 00:45:10,791
I'll give you more than that.

713
00:45:11,542 --> 00:45:14,044
Me too. I can give you more too.

714
00:45:15,212 --> 00:45:16,547
I know.

715
00:45:16,630 --> 00:45:17,881
We're exchanging gifts!

716
00:45:28,392 --> 00:45:29,351
Aunt, here's the phone.

717
00:45:29,893 --> 00:45:30,894
Diego.

718
00:45:31,979 --> 00:45:34,648
We can't lock her up here forever.

719
00:45:36,942 --> 00:45:38,735
I'll think of other plans for Nimfa.

720
00:45:39,194 --> 00:45:41,447
But for now, we can't let her go

721
00:45:41,530 --> 00:45:43,824
because I know
she'll go straight to Emilia.

722
00:45:44,408 --> 00:45:46,118
She'll expose Ivy's identity.

723
00:45:48,871 --> 00:45:50,831
But I know Nimfa's life is in danger too…

724
00:45:51,540 --> 00:45:54,543
once Emilia finds out that
we already know their secret.

725
00:45:56,795 --> 00:46:00,757
If we think about it, Nimfa's
a victim of the Ardientes too.

726
00:46:03,927 --> 00:46:05,429
[phone ringing]

727
00:46:08,807 --> 00:46:10,058
Hello, Marlon.

728
00:46:12,394 --> 00:46:13,729
Do I really need to go there?

729
00:46:14,938 --> 00:46:16,064
All right.

730
00:46:16,732 --> 00:46:19,818
Auntie Camia, I have to go.
Please watch over Nimfa.

731
00:46:20,736 --> 00:46:23,697
All right, I can manage here.
Take care, Diego.

732
00:46:23,780 --> 00:46:24,781
Thank you, Auntie Camia.

733
00:46:36,543 --> 00:46:41,632
Fundraising activities,
national games, Sunday market,

734
00:46:41,715 --> 00:46:42,799
and public dance parties?

735
00:46:42,883 --> 00:46:45,052
How do you expect to raise huge funds

736
00:46:45,135 --> 00:46:47,638
if all you've got are small gimmicks?

737
00:46:48,180 --> 00:46:51,683
Sir, with all due respect,
that's really Diego's branding.

738
00:46:51,767 --> 00:46:54,311
-[Marlon] It courts the masses.
-But we need big ideas.

739
00:46:54,394 --> 00:46:56,271
Tent-pole strategies!

740
00:46:57,064 --> 00:47:00,025
Also, I brought in some new equipment.

741
00:47:00,359 --> 00:47:01,652
It was a donation from the owner

742
00:47:01,735 --> 00:47:04,029
of the largest mall chain in Manila.

743
00:47:04,112 --> 00:47:07,658
Hold on. First of all,
Marlon's the campaign manager.

744
00:47:08,033 --> 00:47:11,787
Secondly, you should inform me
each time you accept a donation.

745
00:47:12,204 --> 00:47:14,540
Because the minute those people
ask me to return the favor,

746
00:47:14,623 --> 00:47:16,375
I can't guarantee that I would.

747
00:47:16,458 --> 00:47:20,254
Relax. I'm the representative
of the party.

748
00:47:20,337 --> 00:47:24,466
And, my job is to ensure that your vision
is aligned with that of the party.

749
00:47:24,550 --> 00:47:26,176
We still have a lot of things to do.

750
00:47:26,718 --> 00:47:29,846
Let's plan our strategies well. Okay?

751
00:47:31,056 --> 00:47:32,057
[Marlon] Okay.

752
00:47:45,487 --> 00:47:47,781
Nimfa? Have something to eat.

753
00:47:50,284 --> 00:47:55,163
No. I need to go home.
Where's my cellphone?

754
00:48:00,294 --> 00:48:03,422
[pensive music playing]

755
00:48:05,507 --> 00:48:07,467
You know, I understand
how you feel, Nimfa.

756
00:48:07,551 --> 00:48:10,095
I also dreamt of having a better life,

757
00:48:10,178 --> 00:48:12,973
and I'd also do anything
for the people I love.

758
00:48:13,515 --> 00:48:15,642
So I understand
why you made that decision.

759
00:48:16,518 --> 00:48:18,103
I know what you're doing.

760
00:48:19,271 --> 00:48:22,566
You're being nice to me
so I won't push through with my plan.

761
00:48:22,649 --> 00:48:25,068
[tense music playing]

762
00:48:25,152 --> 00:48:30,157
I'm still telling Emilia about
the information I discovered!

763
00:48:31,825 --> 00:48:33,368
Now, where's my phone?!

764
00:48:33,452 --> 00:48:36,496
Diego said that we shouldn't let you leave

765
00:48:36,580 --> 00:48:39,625
because he's afraid
of what Emilia could do to you.

766
00:48:39,708 --> 00:48:41,960
Besides, even after
everything you did to us,

767
00:48:43,420 --> 00:48:45,297
we still consider you part of this family.

768
00:48:47,799 --> 00:48:48,800
[sighs]

769
00:48:49,426 --> 00:48:51,053
And we love you.

770
00:48:51,136 --> 00:48:54,181
[tense music playing]

771
00:48:58,268 --> 00:49:00,020
You're a good actress, Camia.

772
00:49:01,605 --> 00:49:04,316
But you still can't fool me.
Get out of my way!

773
00:49:04,399 --> 00:49:06,026
Hey! Stay here!

774
00:49:06,860 --> 00:49:10,572
We're not letting you leave
because we care about you!

775
00:49:10,656 --> 00:49:14,159
Do you understand?!
We're good people, Nimfa!

776
00:49:17,037 --> 00:49:19,665
That's right. You really had me fooled!

777
00:49:21,583 --> 00:49:23,126
-[woman shouts indistinctly]
-Nimfa!

778
00:49:26,296 --> 00:49:27,255
<i>Ivy, it's Nimfa.</i>

779
00:49:27,339 --> 00:49:29,675
<i>She's the one who told Emilia</i>
<i>that Lily is still alive.</i>

780
00:49:29,758 --> 00:49:31,093
[Ivy] <i>Arnaldo.</i>

781
00:49:31,968 --> 00:49:33,887
<i>-Arnaldo.</i>
<i>-Hon, I can explain.</i>

782
00:49:33,970 --> 00:49:35,597
-[grunts]
-<i>Arnaldo!</i>

783
00:49:36,473 --> 00:49:39,351
<i>If you think I'm betraying you,</i>
<i>then I guess, Arnaldo,</i>

784
00:49:39,434 --> 00:49:41,269
<i>we should call off our wedding.</i>

785
00:49:43,313 --> 00:49:45,399
<i>-After her!</i>
<i>-Ma'am Emilia.</i>

786
00:49:45,482 --> 00:49:47,109
<i>So you're Mom's spy.</i>

787
00:49:47,192 --> 00:49:49,528
<i>I need to tell her something</i>
<i>about Miss Ivy.</i>

788
00:49:49,611 --> 00:49:50,570
<i>She's the one feeding…</i>

789
00:49:50,654 --> 00:49:52,072
<i>-information to Diego's camp!</i>
<i>-That's not true!</i>

790
00:49:52,155 --> 00:49:53,657
<i>You need to know that Ivy is--</i>

791
00:49:53,740 --> 00:49:56,868
<i>-That's not true!</i>
-[gunshots]

792
00:49:58,787 --> 00:50:02,082
[theme music playing]
